{
"dur": 47.905,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 5.359,
"text": "It's easy to tell this as a villain story. It's more complicated than that.",
"end": 5.634
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 5.634,
"vo_start": 5.909,
"vo_end": 14.268,
"text": "Index funds have saved ordinary savers huge amounts in fees. A teacher's pension can now own the whole market for almost nothing.",
"end": 14.543
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.543,
"vo_start": 14.818,
"vo_end": 20.418,
"text": "But the same money that makes investing cheap also gathers ownership into a very small number of hands.",
"end": 20.693
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 20.693,
"vo_start": 20.968,
"vo_end": 26.127,
"text": "It began with a young banker who lost a hundred million dollars because he didn't understand his own risk.",
"end": 26.402
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 26.402,
"vo_start": 26.677,
"vo_end": 33.793,
"text": "He built a machine to measure risk, used it to win Washington's trust in 2008, and bought the right business at exactly the right moment.",
"end": 34.068
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 34.068,
"vo_start": 34.343,
"vo_end": 40.943,
"text": "Now the question isn't how BlackRock got so big. It's who should keep watch over a company that owns a piece of everything.",
"end": 41.218
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 41.218,
"vo_start": 41.493,
"vo_end": 46.955,
"text": "If you want to see what happens when one company's product does change the world, watch our story on how Nvidia was built next.",
"end": 47.905
}
],
